{
 "_comment": [
  "CRAFT-UPLIFT look-loop pose set. Frozen: these are the EXACT poses the",
  "purchased-model comparison study (Drive 3dmodels-study-2026-08) used for",
  "its ours/<table>/*.png bank, so every capture here is pixel-comparable",
  "against that bank and against the reference sheets in side-by-side/.",
  "Poses are in the KERNEL frame [kx, ky, h] metres, as __test.cameraPose",
  "consumes them (three.x = k.y, three.y = h, three.z = k.x). fov is",
  "VERTICAL degrees.",
  "Corner anchors are derived, not eyeballed: look = (halfWidth +",
  "cushionWidth, halfLength + cushionWidth) — the outer corner of the",
  "cushion nose chain. Side anchors are the same kx + 4 mm.",
  "predator_apex_9ft reuses the diamond_proam_9ft numbers: both carry a",
  "2.540 x 1.270 m playfield and the same 50.8 mm cushion width, so the",
  "anchor arithmetic lands on the same point. Verified against a live",
  "capture, not assumed (see SPIKE-REPORT-CRAFT.md Phase 0)."
 ],
 "_identity_comment": [
  "MEASURED, not assumed (phase-0 census, /tmp/craft/census.mjs, five live",
  "boots). Three things that look like identity signals are NOT:",
  "  - __test.bed() reports the GAME template, not the rendered table: it",
  "    returns 2.540 x 1.270 on all five boots including chinese8 (whose",
  "    kernel playfield is 2.540 x 1.260) and snooker (3.569 x 1.778).",
  "  - window.__cn8ringtex === 'photo' is true on EVERY table (a module",
  "    global, so the shared chinese8 settle predicate's use of it is a",
  "    texture-readiness signal, not a table signal).",
  "  - window.__snkOccl exists on EVERY table, same reason.",
  "bakeClass+fixture separates three of four, but diamond_proam_9ft and the",
  "silent fallback wpa_generic_9ft are BOTH pool/canopy_panel. So identity",
  "closes on the mesh-name family, which the fallback has none of:",
  "  chinese8 cn8*=259  snooker obSnk*=large  diamond dm*=130",
  "  predator obPdt*=large  wpa_generic_9ft = 0 of any of them."
 ],
